[greg@gagme.uucp (Gregory Gulik) asks:]
>Ok, we've been playing this game here off and on for a couple
>weeks now and we can't figure out one thing.
>what does the color of a potion have to do with it's function?
>Are there any rules for this?
.
a clear potion is always some form of water. other potions are randomly
assigned a color. similarly, scrolls are randomly titled and so on with
rings, amulets and wands, etc. some pieces of armor are randomly named
and others aren't (i.e. an ornamental cope is always an elven cloak
whereas a pair of padded gloves could be one of several things).
weapons have unique descriptions/names.

